        <details>
          <summary>What are the most common reasons for Spain visa rejections?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Top rejection reasons: (1) Insufficient income documentation or unclear income source, (2) Poor quality or missing documents, (3) Income below minimum threshold, (4) Background check issues (criminal records, overstay history), (5) Insurance not recognized or missing copay clause, (6) Insufficient ties to home country (relocation risk), (7) Incomplete applications, (8) Health issues that make you ineligible, (9) Immigration fraud suspicions, (10) Timing (application during government office closures).</p>
