        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Should you appeal a visa rejection or reapply?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Appeal if: (1) You believe the decision is procedurally wrong, (2) New evidence has emerged, (3) The rejection appears arbitrary. Reapply if: (1) You've addressed the core deficiency, (2) You have stronger documentation, (3) The rejection is based on income or document quality (fixable issues). Appeal timelines are 30 days; reapplication can be submitted anytime. Consult an immigration lawyer to determine your best path.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What is the appeal process (recurso de reposición)?</summary>
