        <details>
          <summary>How long does it take to get an appeal decision?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Appeal (recurso de reposición) decisions typically take 6–12 weeks from submission. Administrative appeals move slowly. If you want faster resolution, reapplication often gets a decision faster (4–8 weeks) than appealing. However, appeals are free; reapplication costs money and time preparing documents again. Many people pursue both simultaneously (appeal while preparing reapplication).</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What should you do while waiting for an appeal decision?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>While appealing: (1) Strengthen your documentation for a potential reapplication, (2) Address the core issue identified in your rejection, (3) Gather additional supporting documents, (4) Consider consulting an immigration lawyer about your specific case, (5) Don't travel to Spain while your visa is rejected, (6) Maintain your income/financial position, (7) Continue building your file in case you need to reapply, (8) Monitor email for consulate requests for additional information.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How do you strengthen a reapplication after rejection?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>To strengthen reapplication: (1) Address the stated rejection reason directly with new documentation, (2) If income was questioned, provide 24 months of bank statements instead of 12, (3) If documents were poor quality, resubmit with high-quality scans, (4) Include a cover letter explaining changes or clarifications, (5) Get professional help from an immigration specialist, (6) If background was issue, obtain updated clearance, (7) Include employer/client letters confirming income, (8) Get bank letters verifying consistency of income deposits, (9) Provide detailed explanation of income sources, (10) Wait 30–60 days before reapplying to show consideration of feedback.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
